{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]$ is the *second derivative* of $6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)$.\n\nIn other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]$, which is the derivative of $6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)$.\n\nBecause of this, we need to differentiate $6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)$ twice in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]$:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]=-18\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=6\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=6\\left(-\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(3x+3\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-6\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)\\cdot3\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-18\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\left(\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $-18\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-18\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-54\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-18\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-18\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-18\\left[\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(3x+3\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-18\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\cdot3\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-54\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]=-54\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[6\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)\\right]$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-54\\cos\\left(3x+3\\right)$","correct":true},{"content":"$-18\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{2}{3}\\sin\\left(3x+3\\right)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"